{"id":"CVE-2018-1000187","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-06-05T20:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-17T03:02:32.064Z","description":"A exposure of sensitive information vulnerability exists in Jenkins Kubernetes Plugin 1.7.0 and older in ContainerExecDecorator.java that results in sensitive variables such as passwords being written to logs.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://jenkins.io/security/advisory/2018-06-04/#SECURITY-883","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"vendors":["jenkins","kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1000400","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2018-05-18T18:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T12:40:47.066Z","description":"Kubernetes CRI-O version prior to 1.9 contains a Privilege Context Switching Error (CWE-270) vulnerability in the handling of ambient capabilities that can result in containers running with elevated privileges, allowing users abilities they should not have. This attack appears to be exploitable via container execution. This vulnerability appears to have been fixed in 1.9.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes-incubator/cri-o/pull/1558/files","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/104262","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"104262"}],"vendors":["kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1002100","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2018-06-01T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T16:17:37.665Z","description":"In Kubernetes versions 1.5.x, 1.6.x, 1.7.x, 1.8.x, and prior to version 1.9.6, the kubectl cp command insecurely handles tar data returned from the container, and can be caused to overwrite arbitrary local files.","cwe":["directory traversal vulnerability"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":4.2,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:R/S:U/C:N/I:H/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"Kubernetes","versions":["affected v1.5.x","affected v1.6.x","affected v1.7.x","affected v1.8.x","affected unspecified <v1.9.6 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/61297","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://hansmi.ch/articles/2018-04-openshift-s2i-security","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=1564305","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"credits":["Reported by Michael Hanselmann"],"vendors":["kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1002101","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2018-12-05T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T12:47:57.266Z","description":"In Kubernetes versions 1.9.0-1.9.9, 1.10.0-1.10.5, and 1.11.0-1.11.1, user input was handled insecurely while setting up volume mounts on Windows nodes, which could lead to command line argument injection.","cwe":["argument injection"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":5.9,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"Kubernetes","versions":["affected unspecified <v1.9.10 (custom)","affected unspecified <v1.10.6 (custom)","affected unspecified <v1.11.2 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/65750","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/106238","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"106238"},{"url":"https://security.netapp.com/advisory/ntap-20190416-0008/","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"credits":["Reported by Tim Allclair"],"vendors":["kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1002102","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2019-12-05T16:05:18.042Z","updated":"2024-09-17T00:56:37.681Z","title":"Kubernetes API server follows unvalidated redirects from streaming Kubelet endpoints","description":"Improper validation of URL redirection in the Kubernetes API server in versions prior to v1.14.0 allows an attacker-controlled Kubelet to redirect API server requests from streaming endpoints to arbitrary hosts. Impacted API servers will follow the redirect as a GET request with client-certificate credentials for authenticating to the Kubelet.","cwe":["CWE-601 CWE-601 URL Redirection to Untrusted Site ('Open Redirect')"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":2.6,"sev":"LOW","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:H/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:N/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"Kubernetes","versions":["affected v1.14 <v1.14.0 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/85867","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://lists.fedoraproject.org/archives/list/package-announce%40lists.fedoraproject.org/message/Q56CULSH7F7BC4NPS67ZS23ZCLL5TIVK/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_FEDORA"],"name":"FEDORA-2020-943f4b03d2"}],"workarounds":["For Kubernetes versions >= v1.10.0, the ValidateProxyRedirects feature can be manually enabled with the kube-apiserver flag --feature-gates=ValidateProxyRedirects=true"],"vendors":["kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1002103","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2018-12-05T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-09-16T22:35:01.118Z","description":"In Minikube versions 0.3.0-0.29.0, minikube exposes the Kubernetes Dashboard listening on the VM IP at port 30000. In VM environments where the IP is easy to predict, the attacker can use DNS rebinding to indirectly make requests to the Kubernetes Dashboard, create a new Kubernetes Deployment running arbitrary code. If minikube mount is in use, the attacker could also directly access the host filesystem.","cwe":["Improper Input Validation"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":8.1,"sev":"HIGH","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"Minikube","versions":["affected v0.3.0 <unspecified (custom)","affected unspecified <v0.30.0 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/minikube/issues/3208","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"credits":["Reported by Alex Kaskasoli"],"vendors":["kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1002104","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2020-01-14T20:15:17.491Z","updated":"2024-09-16T21:07:22.919Z","description":"Versions < 1.5 of the Kubernetes ingress default backend, which handles invalid ingress traffic, exposed prometheus metrics publicly.","cwe":["CWE-215 CWE-215 Information Exposure Through Debug Information"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.1","score":5.3,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"k8s.gcr.io/defaultbackend","versions":["affected defaultbackend <1.5 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/pull/3125","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]}],"workarounds":["Mask the /metrics endpoint with an Ingress rule so that metrics aren't exposed publicly. See https://github.com/kubernetes/ingress-nginx/issues/1733#issuecomment-358492359"],"credits":["Alexandre Malucelli"],"vendors":["kubernetes"]}
{"id":"CVE-2018-1002105","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"kubernetes","published":"2018-12-05T21:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-05T12:47:57.159Z","description":"In all Kubernetes versions prior to v1.10.11, v1.11.5, and v1.12.3, incorrect handling of error responses to proxied upgrade requests in the kube-apiserver allowed specially crafted requests to establish a connection through the Kubernetes API server to backend servers, then send arbitrary requests over the same connection directly to the backend, authenticated with the Kubernetes API server's TLS credentials used to establish the backend connection.","cwe":["Unchecked Error Condition"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":9.8,"sev":"CRITICAL","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H"}],"affected":[{"vendor":"Kubernetes","product":"Kubernetes","versions":["affected v1.0.x","affected v1.1.x","affected v1.2.x","affected v1.3.x","affected v1.4.x","affected v1.5.x","affected v1.6.x","affected v1.7.x","affected v1.8.x","affected v1.9.x","affected unspecified <v1.10.11 (custom)","affected unspecified <v1.11.5 (custom)","affected unspecified <v1.12.3 (custom)"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://groups.google.com/forum/#%21topic/kubernetes-announce/GVllWCg6L88","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/46053/","tags":["exploit","x_refsource_EXPLOIT-DB"],"name":"46053"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3549","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3549"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3752","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3752"},{"url":"https://www.exploit-db.com/exploits/46052/","tags":["exploit","x_refsource_EXPLOIT-DB"],"name":"46052"},{"url":"https://access.redhat.com/errata/RHSA-2018:3624","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_REDHAT"],"name":"RHSA-2018:3624"},{"url":"https://www.coalfire.com/The-Coalfire-Blog/December-2018/Kubernetes-Vulnerability-What-You-Can-Shou